Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.02,0:00:06.88,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If you're bored, make me some tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.98,0:00:11.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I can't believe you want \Nhot tea on a day like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.60,0:00:16.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It seems there are signs of \Na strange cult in the castle city lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.41,0:00:19.58,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,I hear they worship a god called Simila.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.90,0:00:23.79,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Right now, they're a minor nuisance at most.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.16,0:00:29.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I have to meet Legis today, so I'll be \Nreturning to Tuldarr for some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.68,0:00:33.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.26,0:00:36.76,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,There's poison in this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.76,0:00:37.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.77,0:00:39.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oh, please don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.03,0:00:42.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Potions have no effect on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.38,0:00:46.35,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The magical power in my body immediately \Nbreaks down their composition.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.35,0:00:48.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.20,0:00:49.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Wait, no, it's not!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.20,0:00:53.48,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,This pitcher was put here\N for Lady Tinasha specifically.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.48,0:00:55.11,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Investigate it at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.42,0:00:59.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,And even in Tuldarr, \Nhave a defensive barrier up at all times.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.74,0:01:01.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.17,0:02:37.01,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Unanswered Prayer ~
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.80,0:02:41.96,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,The water was filled by a lady-in-waiting \Nwho's served the palace for five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.96,0:02:43.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Where did she acquire the poison?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.72,0:02:47.50,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,A mysterious mage handed it \Nto her at the town market.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.50,0:02:51.82,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,He told her that Lady Tinasha was really \Na witch trying to deceive His Majesty...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.56,0:02:56.54,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Oh, Mila.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.54,0:02:57.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.77,0:03:00.07,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha says \Nshe won't be returning tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.37,0:03:03.95,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,It's top secret, but Legis \Nwas attacked and is currently comatose.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.16,0:03:09.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Two of Tuldarr's successors to the throne, \Nattacked on the same day?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.68,0:03:13.77,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,He's in Lady Tinasha's care, \Nso it's not life-threatening,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.77,0:03:16.59,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,but she'll be staying in Tuldarr \Nfor the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.59,0:03:20.05,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Do you think both cases\N share the same culprit?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.52,0:03:23.85,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If so, then they work unusually fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.19,0:03:28.47,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,It's a pleasure to make \Nyour acquaintance, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.47,0:03:31.14,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)}Delilah
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.81,0:03:31.19,Default-Top,Delilah,0,0,0,,My name is Delilah.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.71,0:03:34.46,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,When I heard about the witch's curse \Nplaced on Your Majesty,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.46,0:03:37.15,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,I couldn't stop myself \Nfrom making the journey here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.15,0:03:39.30,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Please let me serve you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.30,0:03:42.86,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,I have the power to withstand the curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.15,0:03:44.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Where did you learn of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.49,0:03:46.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This is a confidential matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.64,0:03:51.33,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,I come from a family of fortune tellers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.33,0:03:53.53,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Our predictions are never wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.28,0:03:59.25,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Fine by me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.25,0:04:00.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We'll prepare a room for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.71,0:04:01.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Live here how you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.97,0:04:03.30,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Please wait a moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.30,0:04:04.27,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,What about Lady Tinasha?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.27,0:04:05.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's enough out of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.89,0:04:07.34,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This is my decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.34,0:04:08.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Do any of you object?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.27,0:04:14.73,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,We received word from Tuldarr that \Nthey've arrested Prince Legis's attacker.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.08,0:04:18.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Her spirit came to tell me directly as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.97,0:04:24.22,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,But it seems there's no connection \Nto the mage who tried to poison Lady Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.22,0:04:25.56,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Sounds like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.05,0:04:29.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's with the gloomy look?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.44,0:04:30.87,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Cut it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.94,0:04:32.87,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.87,0:04:36.96,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,With all due respect, I don't approve \Nof that woman being at your side.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.04,0:04:41.24,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you're trying \Nto provoke Lady Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.24,0:04:43.81,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I wouldn't do that and risk \Nhaving her destroy the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.81,0:04:45.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's too eccentric, even for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.88,0:04:47.81,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Anyway, just leave it be.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.81,0:04:50.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I hear Legis's treatment will take some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.81,0:05:00.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha, you're back?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.75,0:05:03.03,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Long time no see.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.36,0:05:05.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,How's Legis doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.10,0:05:06.99,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Fortunately, he's recovered.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.99,0:05:08.16,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.16,0:05:10.48,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,I've called over a tailor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.48,0:05:12.82,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,If you'd like, please join me...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.41,0:05:16.45,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,I haven't seen you around here before.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.45,0:05:18.28,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Are you a mage of some kind?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.28,0:05:20.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.34,0:05:22.56,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,My name is Tinasha, and I come from Tuldarr.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.65,0:05:25.23,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Well, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.23,0:05:28.94,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,So you're the princess of Tuldarr?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.81,0:05:34.84,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,You seem to be quite close with that woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.84,0:05:37.12,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,You should choose your friends more wisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.31,0:05:40.19,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What are you implying?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.54,0:05:46.40,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Befriending Tuldarr royalty \Nmust come with lots of benefits, indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.15,0:05:48.61,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,I would never...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.57,0:05:54.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Um, you seem to be offering advice \Nwithout even introducing yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.80,0:05:56.79,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,And who exactly might you be?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.51,0:06:02.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I won't tolerate anyone \Nwho insults a friend of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.92,0:06:07.84,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How about you look in the mirror \Nbefore giving other people advice?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.50,0:06:12.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Go easy on the intimidation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.40,0:06:13.59,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She's my lover.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.22,0:06:19.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.80,0:06:22.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So that insolent woman is his mistress.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.90,0:06:25.40,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Well, you know about His Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.40,0:06:28.36,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,She claims she can withstand it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.64,0:06:30.13,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,By "it", you mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.13,0:06:32.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's impossible for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.05,0:06:33.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,She's sure to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.65,0:06:36.41,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,What? Y-You mean it? I'll let His Majesty...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.41,0:06:38.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They both gave their consent, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.13,0:06:43.66,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I feel like...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.66,0:06:45.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I've been a fool this whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.13,0:06:53.46,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar, you idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.22,0:06:58.04,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,After saying you'd make sure I was happy...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.99,0:07:06.12,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I like the look on your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.73,0:07:08.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Travis.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.10,0:07:10.21,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,What's it been, four hundred years?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.21,0:07:13.45,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Looks like you traveled through time, \Nthanks to my tips.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.45,0:07:15.68,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,How'd it go with that man?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.16,0:07:18.53,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.53,0:07:22.82,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,You fell into a magic slumber to meet him, \Nand he shows no interest in you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.82,0:07:24.00,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,How sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.64,0:07:27.88,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Why don't you just kill her?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.39,0:07:32.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Humans aren't supposed to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.48,0:07:34.94,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Humans are the only ones who ever do.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.10,0:07:40.20,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,If you won't kill her, would you rather die?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.20,0:07:41.77,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Since you're suffering as is.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.77,0:07:42.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.23,0:07:48.04,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.04,0:07:49.78,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,He's made me his mistress.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.28,0:07:54.04,Italics,Old Man,0,0,0,,It looks like poison doesn't work \Non Tuldarr's princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.04,0:07:56.66,Italics,Old Man,0,0,0,,If you can, have her removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.66,0:07:58.99,Italics,Old Man,0,0,0,,Can you get in the treasury?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.99,0:08:01.21,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,I think I can, if I ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.21,0:08:02.89,Italics,Old Man,0,0,0,,Be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.89,0:08:04.96,Italics,Old Man,0,0,0,,If you make it in, look for a box.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.96,0:08:08.17,Italics,Old Man,0,0,0,,One containing a small orb \Netched with a pattern.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.28,0:08:14.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You were quite the cautious one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.68,0:08:17.22,Default,Delilah,0,0,0,,Y-Your Majesty! You have the wrong idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.22,0:08:20.39,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll receive a report later to see \Nwho drove you to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.39,0:08:23.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I already have someone \Nworking to break my curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.40,0:08:27.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She may be odd, but she's a fine woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.51,0:08:30.51,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I've got my hands full with her.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.71,0:08:37.03,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Done already?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.36,0:08:39.43,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I shouldn't have gotten my hopes up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.43,0:08:40.49,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,As for the rest...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.97,0:08:43.36,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'll have that man of yours pay instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.97,0:08:48.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I won't let you get close to him!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.67,0:08:49.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Take form!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.27,0:09:00.18,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.96,0:09:13.02,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't want to die yet...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.39,0:09:17.95,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,As for who Delilah was communicating with,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.95,0:09:20.31,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,they're in a building in the Farsas castle city.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.02,0:09:23.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That shady cult, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.71,0:09:25.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Head there at once and round them all up.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.70,0:09:26.91,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't let anyone slip away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.91,0:09:27.62,Default,Group,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.40,0:09:30.29,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.29,0:09:31.30,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.30,0:09:34.90,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,I just felt a powerful surge \Nof magic from the north.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.90,0:09:37.48,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,It's on the level of a forbidden curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.48,0:09:38.56,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.29,0:09:41.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Where's Tinasha?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.47,0:09:42.50,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Come help!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.50,0:09:44.60,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha's going to die!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.34,0:09:52.98,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,The hubby's here already?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.39,0:09:57.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.74,0:10:10.29,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I wouldn't swing that sword so wantonly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.29,0:10:11.50,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,It's dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.92,0:10:13.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What did you do to her?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.77,0:10:14.83,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Nothing much.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.83,0:10:16.42,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,We just had a little fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.25,0:10:20.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't think you can escape alive, monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.72,0:10:23.26,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,You can tell I'm not human?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.26,0:10:24.36,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,How amusing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.98,0:10:28.67,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Her barrier, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.73,0:10:34.40,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Enough of your mockery.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.40,0:10:37.21,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'll burn you alive until nothing remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.29,0:10:39.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I won't let you kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.92,0:10:41.85,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.75,0:10:48.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I won't let you lay a finger on him,\Nno matter the cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.54,0:10:51.56,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,What a fool you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.56,0:10:54.00,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,All that, for someone \Nwho shows no interest in you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.44,0:10:55.77,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,How pointless.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.06,0:11:01.23,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'm tired.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.23,0:11:03.13,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'll play with you some other day.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.50,0:11:11.73,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,We arrested all the leaders of the cult \Nthat sent Delilah to the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.73,0:11:15.94,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,But you didn't find the mage \Nwho gave that servant the poison?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.94,0:11:19.78,Default,Als,0,0,0,,To summarize what we know, \Nthey have two motives.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.78,0:11:22.91,Default,Als,0,0,0,,First, to seize a mysterious orb \Nthey say is in the treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.36,0:11:28.23,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Second, to assassinate Lady Tinasha, \Nor drive her away from this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.22,0:11:32.86,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We'll have to sort through the treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.57,0:11:35.16,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Something feels off...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.32,0:11:38.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.95,0:11:42.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Um... I have a favor to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.21,0:11:43.16,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Out with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.37,0:11:47.39,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Teach me how to use a sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.62,0:11:55.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are your injuries healed?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.26,0:11:56.11,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.11,0:12:00.53,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Well, rather than healed, I think \NTravis regrew all the parts I'd lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.83,0:12:02.25,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Regrew it all?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.84,0:12:05.99,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What {\i1}is{\i0} that monster Travis, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.99,0:12:08.40,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,He's one of the highest-ranking demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.40,0:12:10.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,In common parlance, a demon king.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.54,0:12:15.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That aside, why did you tie up that woman?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.34,0:12:17.17,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Did you two have a lovers' spat?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.17,0:12:18.99,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.99,0:12:21.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I was leading her on from the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.26,0:12:24.38,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I had my suspicions the moment \Nshe mentioned my curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.67,0:12:28.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It ended up being the same group \Nthat tried to poison you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.70,0:12:31.35,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You should have told me that from the start.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.65,0:12:33.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If I had known, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.34,0:12:35.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Wouldn't have shattered any windows?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.40,0:12:38.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I didn't shatter any this time!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.38,0:12:43.64,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That reminds me, when we fought \Nagainst Druza, I borrowed your vision.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.64,0:12:46.38,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Can anyone see like you do \Nwith enough practice?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.78,0:12:49.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's impossible unless you're born with it,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.07,0:12:50.67,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but you have the potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.48,0:12:52.25,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.25,0:12:54.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If you develop the awareness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.29,0:12:57.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That can be something \NI teach you some other time.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.96,0:12:58.94,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.04,0:13:05.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I will say though, \Nyou have the fundamentals down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.97,0:13:10.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Before I was crowned queen, I received \Na short crash course in swordplay.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.02,0:13:13.53,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's fairly traditional Farsas technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.22,0:13:15.70,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How can you tell?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.70,0:13:17.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's absolutely right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.15,0:13:23.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Must have been an odd fellow, \Nteaching a trueborn mage to use a sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.25,0:13:28.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,He was a strict but kind man.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.06,0:13:40.04,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,How did it go, Valt?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.04,0:13:41.92,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,A failure on both ends.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.92,0:13:43.00,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,They were captured.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.53,0:13:44.81,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Is that really okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.81,0:13:46.01,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.27,0:13:51.22,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Powerful as she may be, she's a lot easier \Nto handle than when she was a witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.79,0:13:54.04,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,This has never happened before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.70,0:13:59.31,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Here's a list of all\N the articles in the treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.31,0:14:01.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This is going to be a pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.66,0:14:04.30,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Once we've had trustworthy \Npeople verify all the items,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.30,0:14:06.11,Default,Als,0,0,0,,we'll seal off the underground labyrinth.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.11,0:14:09.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,There's a labyrinth under the castle?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.07,0:14:12.59,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Forty years ago, \Na burglar got into the treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.18,0:14:16.58,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,They made an escape, \Nand no one found out what they took.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.58,0:14:21.54,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The king at the time, my grandfather, \Nwas quite distraught.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.54,0:14:23.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So he built a labyrinth?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.75,0:14:27.05,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,He built it so that once someone enters,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.05,0:14:30.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,the doors can't be opened for a full day \Nby anyone outside the royal family.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.26,0:14:32.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Even royalty can't open it \Nfrom the inside for a full day.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.50,0:14:36.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I suppose it really does run in the family.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.06,0:14:37.61,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Did you say something?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.30,0:14:41.98,Default,Als,0,0,0,,So you take no issue to the labyrinth \Nbeing sealed off as planned?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.34,0:14:43.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Let me see...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.23,0:14:48.90,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1000,1)}Underground Labyrinth    {\fs14}Depths of the Farsas Treasury
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.81,0:14:48.90,Default-Top,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I swear...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.90,0:14:51.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You really can be unreasonable at times.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.81,0:14:53.87,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Think of it as practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.61,0:14:58.34,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This path seems pretty straight \Nfor a labyrinth, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.92,0:15:02.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I bet he just wanted to call it a labyrinth.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.16,0:15:07.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What's a lake doing under the castle?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.41,0:15:11.53,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What's more, I sense something ominous.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.25,0:15:16.14,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Could this be the Lake of Silence?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.14,0:15:19.14,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)}Lake of Silence
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.41,0:15:19.14,Default-Top,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What exactly is the Lake of Silence?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.14,0:15:21.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's from an old Farsas legend.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.41,0:15:24.18,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,An inhuman creature is said to have \Npulled Akashia from the lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.86,0:15:28.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The people drew close \Nand settled in its vicinity, or so it goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.49,0:15:30.06,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I was sure it was just myth.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.66,0:15:33.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I can't believe \Nthey built a castle on top of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.67,0:15:39.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's a door doing there?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.50,0:15:45.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.41,0:15:52.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.34,0:16:12.49,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.11,0:16:14.48,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.94,0:16:17.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I think I broke some ribs.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.95,0:16:19.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Can you heal yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.82,0:16:23.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Actually, it looks like I can't use magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.61,0:16:26.13,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.53,0:16:28.19,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,This lake water...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.19,0:16:32.20,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It must contain some \Nof the same material as Akashia.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.20,0:16:36.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Drinking it disturbs the magic in your body, \Nmaking you unable to cast spells.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.11,0:16:45.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This looks a little familiar.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.19,0:16:56.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What is this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.83,0:17:00.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Basically, this has got to be \NGrandpa's hideout.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.03,0:17:05.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If it has fresh water, \NI'd like to wash this water off.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.26,0:17:09.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Feeling better?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.74,0:17:11.63,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes, this should do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.35,0:17:16.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That reminds me, why are you \Ngoing through the treasury all of a sudden?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.08,0:17:17.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Looking for something?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.65,0:17:20.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Oh, I guess I never told you about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.89,0:17:25.95,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That shady cult was after \Nsomething in this treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.95,0:17:28.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We're not sure what exactly it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.88,0:17:31.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Apparently, it's a red orb \Nthat fits in your palm.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.47,0:17:35.28,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.28,0:17:36.99,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Don't touch that orb!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.31,0:17:38.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.04,0:17:39.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Don't let anyone touch it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.83,0:17:44.66,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,No, don't look for it...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.82,0:17:50.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Don't leave me...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.26,0:17:51.25,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.23,0:17:55.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You should tell me if you've got a fever!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.97,0:18:01.13,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.71,0:18:04.84,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The same orb exists in Tuldarr as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.45,0:18:07.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,One of a different color.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.14,0:18:08.63,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.09,0:18:14.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I sealed away the one in Tuldarr \Nfour hundred years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.33,0:18:15.78,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Sealed it away?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.78,0:18:17.30,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Is it dangerous?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.21,0:18:22.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It holds an incredible power, \Nunprecedented in magical history.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.30,0:18:26.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That orb sends its user into the past,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.54,0:18:30.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,a feat no mage or demon is capable of.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.09,0:18:34.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It does sound dangerous, \Nbut can't it be useful when used right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.44,0:18:35.77,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Not exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.20,0:18:41.23,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,When you use it, everything you have \Nis erased as you go back in time,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.23,0:18:44.11,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and you must rebuild it all \Nfrom the very beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.73,0:18:51.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,When I was a child, \Nthere was someone who saved my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.50,0:18:54.63,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But the price he paid
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.94,0:19:00.66,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,was giving up everything he had, \Nfrom his past to his future.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.49,0:19:04.94,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So that was the man who saved your life?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.98,0:19:14.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I won't leave you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.97,0:19:16.63,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I don't want to change the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.38,0:19:19.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I won't look for the orb \Nif you don't want me to,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.65,0:19:21.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,and I'm okay with sealing it away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.51,0:19:25.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So don't you ever cry like that again.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.14,0:19:34.16,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If this was my grandfather's hideout,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.16,0:19:37.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,there should be a shortcut that \Ndoesn't pass through the treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.64,0:19:44.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,"Don't leave me," huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.09,0:19:50.15,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.30,0:19:57.30,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha, we can go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.12,0:20:04.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You already knew my name the moment we met.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.46,0:20:13.39,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Why must you come in through the window?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.81,0:20:16.58,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are your broken bones healed?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.58,0:20:18.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm all better.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.64,0:20:20.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Sorry to worry you like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.35,0:20:27.39,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Actually, when I brought you back, \Neveryone was mad at me, even Als.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.86,0:20:30.13,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.13,0:20:31.95,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,No, it was my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.58,0:20:35.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So what do we do with that orb?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.37,0:20:36.79,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We can seal it away if you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.79,0:20:39.79,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Isn't it an heirloom from your mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.79,0:20:42.13,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,An heirloom? My mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.65,0:20:44.59,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll ask my father.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.59,0:20:46.58,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.32,0:20:54.63,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.63,0:20:56.83,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I don't know anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.83,0:20:58.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,And I don't need to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.21,0:21:01.88,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Everything I've done is by my own choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.88,0:21:04.85,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I have no complaints or regrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.85,0:21:08.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The same holds true for every choice I make, \Nregardless of time or place.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.27,0:21:11.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So stop feeling sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.33,0:21:12.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.85,0:21:14.15,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You figured it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.61,0:21:23.13,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm glad I came to this age and met you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.67,0:21:29.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's only been four months since I woke up, \Nbut you've made me so happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.97,0:21:39.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,This is enough for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.90,0:21:43.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,In the future, even if we part ways,
